WEBVTT

00:02.820 --> 00:07.180
You said that I killed Orobas...

00:07.180 --> 00:08.440
Th-That's right!

00:08.710 --> 00:10.700
You're mistaken.

00:10.700 --> 00:16.000
The great dragon could never be laid 
low by one with my meager strength.

00:16.000 --> 00:18.310
You're lying! I saw it!

00:18.310 --> 00:21.330
You were devouring my father's corpse!

00:21.760 --> 00:24.460
You had to have tricked him somehow!

00:24.460 --> 00:28.180
Let me ask you, then... 
Was the Orobas you knew

00:28.180 --> 00:32.880
so feeble that he could be 
killed by human treachery?

00:33.440 --> 00:34.760
What do you mean?

00:35.880 --> 00:39.570
I sought out the Sage Dragon, Orobas,

00:39.570 --> 00:42.480
on that day in order to 
slay a particular foe.

00:42.820 --> 00:46.310
And in his magnanimity, he offered his help.

00:46.990 --> 00:47.940
What foe?

00:48.480 --> 00:52.860
A demon. The entities spoken of in legends.

00:54.810 --> 00:58.380
Do you really think you can fool me
 with this made-up nonsense?!

00:58.380 --> 01:01.200
The idea of demons still existing...

01:01.750 --> 01:04.560
I understand your reluctance to believe it.

01:04.560 --> 01:08.580
I, too, had thought they 
were consigned to history.

01:08.980 --> 01:11.980
But... a demon had appeared in modern times,

01:11.980 --> 01:15.670
with many Angelic Knights and the 
great dragon paying the price.

01:16.750 --> 01:21.340
And it's likely that they will
return in force in the near future.

01:25.770 --> 01:28.270
I encountered the shadow of a demon.

01:29.770 --> 01:32.720
I don't know if they intend on
 coming back to this world,

01:32.720 --> 01:35.720
but they do still exist out there somewhere.

01:36.150 --> 01:41.410
That's why I've been looking through old texts:
 to find a way to counter them.

01:41.860 --> 01:43.740
You were helping with that, remember?

01:44.770 --> 01:49.870
Then... Then my father 
fought and lost to a demon?

01:49.870 --> 01:51.530
He was not defeated.

01:52.380 --> 01:55.460
He overcame his enemy 
at the cost of his life.

01:55.760 --> 02:00.340
Then who am I supposed to hate?!

02:00.880 --> 02:04.060
You should not feel hate, but pride.

02:05.690 --> 02:10.650
Orobas gave his life to defend you 
and the world in which you live.

02:10.990 --> 02:14.650
And who better to take 
pride in that than you?

02:15.140 --> 02:18.200
If killing me will restore 
your pride in Orobas...

02:18.800 --> 02:20.990
Then I gladly offer my head.

02:22.280 --> 02:23.780
The demons are a menace.

02:24.200 --> 02:27.820
If they were to return to our world, where the
 Church and sorcerers fight among themselves,

02:27.820 --> 02:29.660
humanity stands no chance.

02:29.660 --> 02:31.250
Preparations must be made.

02:31.670 --> 02:35.750
That was why Orobas told me to go on living.

02:36.210 --> 02:38.660
Which is what led me to 
do something as foul

02:38.660 --> 02:42.760
as drink his blood in the midst 
of that horrible battlefield.

02:44.400 --> 02:46.680
<i>That explains what For saw.</i>

02:47.230 --> 02:50.240
My duty is coming to an end, though.

02:50.240 --> 02:52.720
The seeds of reconciliation 
have finally bloomed.

02:52.720 --> 02:57.080
I can think of no finer last mission 
than to die in the name of Orobas.

02:57.730 --> 03:02.700
Then she was right, you really were the 
one behind the reconciliation faction.

03:03.060 --> 03:04.240
Aye.

03:04.240 --> 03:09.220
The millennia-long vendetta between 
the Church and sorcerers must end,

03:09.220 --> 03:11.430
so that both can survive the coming storm.

03:11.430 --> 03:15.790
Come on, man, you can't 
expect anyone to buy that.

03:16.230 --> 03:20.590
Do you realize how many hundreds of
 dead sorcerers' blood is on your hands?

03:20.590 --> 03:22.980
And now you're all about coexistence?

03:22.980 --> 03:26.810
You're right. I could never bear 
the flag of reconciliation.

03:27.590 --> 03:28.680
Which is why...

03:29.100 --> 03:31.750
the Maiden of the Sacred Sword was necessary!

03:31.750 --> 03:33.600
W-Wait a moment...

03:34.240 --> 03:37.540
I still haven't agreed to any of this!

03:43.670 --> 03:48.830
It feels like the world has an
 excess of immortals lately.

03:49.230 --> 03:51.240
I'm going to take care of it again.

03:51.240 --> 03:52.620
It shouldn't take long.

03:53.180 --> 03:54.210
What are you going to do?

03:54.650 --> 03:56.630
Golems aren't my area of expertise,

03:57.130 --> 03:59.440
but this thing was still made with sorcery.

03:59.440 --> 04:00.880
I should be able to break it.

04:00.880 --> 04:03.050
That is no mere golem.

04:03.840 --> 04:09.390
It's a sorcerous combination of 
a golem and something else.

04:09.690 --> 04:10.520
Are you saying...

04:11.010 --> 04:11.980
Aye.

04:12.470 --> 04:15.980
A chimera, made from a demon!

04:15.980 --> 04:20.990
<b>Episode 11:
 It's Still Apparently an Angelic Knight's 
Duty To Slay Wicked Beasts</b>

04:23.520 --> 04:27.660
I'm sure of it. That is the very 
same demon that Orobas and I slew.

04:27.660 --> 04:33.580
Archdemon Marchosias took its 
carcass and made it into a chimera.

04:35.480 --> 04:39.710
<i>Damn it, Marchosias, I can't think of a more 
dangerous memento to have left behind.</i>

04:40.180 --> 04:42.710
<i>Re-animated corpse or not, 
this thing is still a demon.</i>

04:42.710 --> 04:45.200
<i>It may not be as strong as it once was,</i>

04:45.200 --> 04:48.320
<i>but it stands to reason that just 
punching it won't make it fall apart.</i>

04:48.880 --> 04:50.060
How convenient.

04:50.420 --> 04:53.280
Now I can test out the other aspect.

04:55.260 --> 04:59.800
Zagan, I won't ask you to trust 
in me, an Angelic Knight...

04:59.800 --> 05:01.530
But let me fight at your side.

05:01.910 --> 05:05.780
I don't really think you're clever 
enough to be scheming, anyway.

05:05.780 --> 05:09.620
Is that a compliment or an insult?!

05:09.620 --> 05:10.490
Good question.

05:11.260 --> 05:12.200
Regardless...

05:13.100 --> 05:14.960
I'll clear your path!

05:17.200 --> 05:18.540
No more doubts.

05:19.810 --> 05:21.820
So, lend me your strength...

05:22.550 --> 05:24.340
Sacred Sword Azrael!

05:30.660 --> 05:32.060
<i>Purifying flames.</i>

05:32.580 --> 05:35.690
<i>But hers aren't as wild as Raphael's.</i>

05:35.690 --> 05:37.730
<i>They cling more tightly to the blade.</i>

05:41.080 --> 05:42.190
Idiot, what are you—?!

05:42.190 --> 05:44.530
You're not wearing your
 anointed armor! You'll die!

05:44.530 --> 05:47.110
I told you I would clear your path!

05:48.320 --> 05:49.320
Here it comes!

05:49.740 --> 05:51.200
I know!

05:58.920 --> 06:00.380
Now, run, Zagan!

06:00.710 --> 06:03.460
Bold of you to give me orders!

06:16.930 --> 06:20.350
<i>This black haze must be its essence.</i>

06:20.350 --> 06:23.020
<i>Which explains how it can re-form 
even if its stone body is shattered.</i>

06:23.020 --> 06:24.730
Keep moving, Zagan!

06:31.440 --> 06:32.530
<i>So fast!</i>

06:32.860 --> 06:36.950
<i>If she had done that when we 
first met, she might've killed me!</i>

06:37.550 --> 06:38.830
<i>But now...</i>

06:42.370 --> 06:44.930
Incinerate, Heaven's Phosphor!

06:43.920 --> 06:45.750
<b>Heaven's
Phosphor</b>

06:47.670 --> 06:48.470
Did it misfire?

06:49.010 --> 06:49.950
No.

06:55.840 --> 06:57.180
The fight's over.

07:00.900 --> 07:02.400
What did you do?

07:02.980 --> 07:05.440
There's a sorcery I named Heaven's Scale...

07:05.850 --> 07:10.190
It's a shield that absorbs mana from its 
surroundings to increase its durability,

07:10.880 --> 07:14.620
so I inverted it and cast 
it inside of that creature.

07:14.980 --> 07:16.590
You inverted it?

07:16.590 --> 07:20.290
It absorbs mana from its 
surroundings and then ignites it.

07:20.730 --> 07:24.750
The black flames are a sign 
that mana itself is the fuel.

07:24.750 --> 07:32.260
<b>Heaven's 
Phosphor</b>

07:24.750 --> 07:32.260
<b>Heaven's 
Scale</b>

07:25.220 --> 07:29.120
Heaven's Scale and Heaven's Phosphor. 
A two-in-one sorcery.

07:29.120 --> 07:32.260
Put together to defend against 
Sacred Swords and demons...

07:32.610 --> 07:35.100
That said, it's still lacking in efficiency.

07:35.100 --> 07:38.520
It needs improvement if I want it 
to affect an actual demon.

07:38.960 --> 07:42.140
You really are one dreadful sorcerer.

07:42.710 --> 07:46.400
You're stronger than 
I thought, too, Chastille.

07:46.650 --> 07:47.650
<b>Daze...</b>

07:47.650 --> 07:48.390
What is it?

07:48.390 --> 07:52.950
Well... you've never actually 
called me by name before.

07:52.950 --> 07:56.080
I haven't? Sorry about that.

07:56.080 --> 07:57.780
You'd actually apologize?!

07:58.370 --> 08:01.100
You're one of Nephy's friends.

08:01.100 --> 08:02.750
You're owed at least that much respect.

08:03.120 --> 08:04.000
<b>Hmph</b>

08:04.300 --> 08:07.430
I didn't come here exclusively 
for Nephy's sake!

08:08.020 --> 08:10.760
I can fight by your side.

08:11.210 --> 08:13.380
When we're a sorcerer and a Angelic Knight?

08:13.790 --> 08:16.390
Even if we're a sorcerer 
and a Angelic Knight!

08:17.450 --> 08:24.020
<i>Well, it does feel nice having someone 
I can trust to watch my back.</i>

08:24.020 --> 08:25.080
Zagan!

08:29.520 --> 08:33.820
I have just borne witness to the 
swiftest blade among the Angelic Knights.

08:35.000 --> 08:38.740
Don't talk too much. 
Healing sorcery isn't my forte.

08:39.170 --> 08:40.940
<i>The wound's too deep.</i>

08:40.940 --> 08:43.570
<i>His draconic regeneration 
seems to be weaker, too.</i>

08:44.070 --> 08:45.420
Chastille...

08:46.290 --> 08:48.430
Regardless of how you may feel about it,

08:48.430 --> 08:53.380
your very actions have made 
you the symbol of our cause.

08:53.950 --> 08:59.050
Those who share my views 
will lend you their strength.

08:59.620 --> 09:03.320
Then the reason you used Orobas' name...

09:03.320 --> 09:05.980
It was because no one would have 
believed you were behind it?

09:06.440 --> 09:08.650
That is part of it. But more than that...

09:09.050 --> 09:12.800
Creating the reconciliation 
faction was Orobas' idea.

09:12.800 --> 09:15.650
My continued survival is thanks to him.

09:16.230 --> 09:20.780
I couldn't think of a better 
name for our leader.

09:21.160 --> 09:22.280
I see.

09:22.280 --> 09:23.420
In that case,

09:24.170 --> 09:27.420
why have you killed so many sorcerers?

09:27.420 --> 09:29.660
Do you have some kind of 
vendetta against them?

09:29.660 --> 09:32.500
I wish I hadn't killed them.

09:32.970 --> 09:36.430
But for some reason,
 they would always attack me.

09:38.130 --> 09:39.430
I can't understand why.

09:40.220 --> 09:43.640
It was always my intention to 
have a friendly dialogue...

09:44.480 --> 09:47.360
I would even laugh to demonstrate 
my lack of ill will,

09:47.360 --> 09:51.520
but the sorcerers would always 
attack as if they were threatened!

09:51.520 --> 09:57.570
<b>Wauuugh!</b>

09:51.520 --> 09:57.570
<b>Get him!</b>

09:51.870 --> 09:54.010
Get him!

09:54.010 --> 09:57.570
Of course, I had to defend myself.

09:57.570 --> 10:00.320
Which is how I ended up cutting them down.

10:00.320 --> 10:01.950
Hang on a second.

10:02.440 --> 10:08.370
Do you realize how antagonistic you 
came across at the bar where we met?!

10:08.370 --> 10:12.850
But I was warning you of the danger 
to Chastille, your acquaintance?

10:12.850 --> 10:14.100
That's what you thought?!

10:14.100 --> 10:20.240
Didn't you ask me how many sorcerers 
I'd killed when we first met?!

10:20.240 --> 10:23.610
Well, you couldn't serve as the head of the 
movement if you'd been acting as I had.

10:23.610 --> 10:27.100
And you answered that it was a 
number one shouldn't take pride in!

10:27.590 --> 10:30.390
That was when I became sure 
that you were the one!

10:30.390 --> 10:31.730
Do you understand tone?!

10:33.300 --> 10:37.230
You need to take a good look 
at yourself in the mirror!

10:37.230 --> 10:42.380
If you act like that while looking like that,
 anybody would assume you're the bad guy!

10:42.380 --> 10:44.310
<i>You're</i> saying that? Seriously?

10:45.910 --> 10:47.250
<b>Ow</b>

10:46.280 --> 10:47.250
Ow.

10:47.520 --> 10:50.250
Return to the Church, Chastille.

10:50.640 --> 10:54.630
I will deal with those who'd 
seek to eliminate you.

10:54.630 --> 10:58.370
I'm sure I can last at least that long.

10:58.370 --> 11:01.390
You know who tried to kill me?

11:02.050 --> 11:04.890
I'd be surprised if you had no idea, frankly.

11:09.180 --> 11:14.020
Child of Orobas... I beg that you claim my head 
only after this last task is finished.

11:14.420 --> 11:15.940
Tell me one thing.

11:16.810 --> 11:20.740
What kind of dragon do you think Orobas was?

11:22.980 --> 11:24.700
A grand one.

11:25.130 --> 11:29.120
The moments I spent upon his back,
 fighting alongside him...

11:29.730 --> 11:32.830
may have been the most 
profound in my entire life.

11:42.940 --> 11:44.150
Are you sure about this?

11:44.630 --> 11:45.930
I don't know.

11:46.260 --> 11:51.100
I don't know if killing him 
is right anymore, either.

11:51.520 --> 11:53.850
I'd say you did the right thing, then.

11:58.250 --> 12:01.860
Let's head home. 
I'm sure Nephy's waiting for us.

12:06.730 --> 12:11.240
<i>I don't know if giving up on 
revenge is the right decision.</i>

12:12.100 --> 12:15.520
<i>Her hatred may grow more bitter in time.</i>

12:15.520 --> 12:17.300
<i>She may be unsure of the decision.</i>

12:17.780 --> 12:18.590
<i>But even if she does...</i>

12:24.130 --> 12:26.550
Welcome home, Lord Zagan.

12:26.950 --> 12:32.250
Welcome back, For, 
Miss Chastille, Lord Barbatos.

12:32.250 --> 12:33.270
We're back.

12:34.330 --> 12:39.020
<i>Nephy and I have decided to 
stand at this girl's side.</i>

12:39.020 --> 12:44.030
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

12:46.780 --> 12:50.410
Then you still haven't found Chastille.

12:50.710 --> 12:53.960
Please forgive our failure, Your Eminence.

12:54.320 --> 12:57.660
This was not your failing.

12:57.660 --> 13:01.050
I, too, am concerned for 
Chastille's well-being.

13:01.370 --> 13:05.170
It's late for the evening. 
Take to your rest for now.

13:05.170 --> 13:05.800
Yes, sir!

13:08.420 --> 13:10.560
<i>Oh, Chastille.</i>

13:11.210 --> 13:12.980
<i>My knight...</i>

13:14.750 --> 13:15.980
<i>Why?</i>

13:16.740 --> 13:20.020
Why won't you just die?!

13:20.810 --> 13:22.750
Sorcerers are evil!

13:23.390 --> 13:25.700
As are those who would side with them!

13:26.640 --> 13:29.610
If it weren't for the objections 
of the other cardinals,

13:29.610 --> 13:31.990
she would've been executed by now!

13:32.540 --> 13:36.160
And now that man had to stick 
his nose into this matter!

13:36.610 --> 13:40.420
Resulting in two of the
 Sacred Swords being unaccounted for.

13:40.960 --> 13:44.630
Curse the wench! 
Did the poison not kill her?!

13:45.060 --> 13:50.640
If Chastille had died, the Sacred Sword 
would have passed into new hands, free of sin.

13:51.000 --> 13:54.020
Much like it has before...

13:54.410 --> 13:58.520
Those unworthy of the Sacred Swords have 
been struck down in the name of righteousness.

13:58.520 --> 14:01.610
The fools who dare defy me

14:01.610 --> 14:05.060
and the cowards who
 hesitate to slay sinners...

14:05.060 --> 14:06.770
They shall all face my wrath.

14:10.110 --> 14:11.910
Pardon the intrusion, Clavwell.

14:12.230 --> 14:15.320
Sir Raphael! What happened to your arm?!

14:15.320 --> 14:16.750
Don't worry about it.

14:16.750 --> 14:20.070
I just came by to tie up a loose end.

14:20.070 --> 14:22.460
Don't be ridiculous! You need treatment.

14:24.770 --> 14:28.470
<i>This is it. I have no idea what he's after,</i>

14:28.470 --> 14:31.110
<i>but this man is a sinner, too...</i>

14:31.600 --> 14:33.930
Quickly, let me apply this 
medicine to your wound.

14:39.710 --> 14:41.150
Unfortunately for you,

14:41.150 --> 14:45.320
I'm not inclined to be touched 
by hands drenched in poison.

14:49.930 --> 14:51.720
Quiet down!

14:51.720 --> 14:55.490
Believe it or not, this will be the first time
 I've gone out of my way to kill someone.

14:55.760 --> 14:57.660
So I'm a bit nervous.

14:58.110 --> 15:00.320
You and I are both past our prime.

15:00.320 --> 15:04.230
We shouldn't interfere with 
the younger generation.

15:04.230 --> 15:08.170
And the idea of snuffing out a 
promising future is out of the question!

15:08.170 --> 15:10.460
<i>Someone! Save me!</i>

15:10.460 --> 15:14.180
<i>I speak in God's name! I am 
the executor of His justice!</i>

15:14.470 --> 15:16.720
<i>Someone! Where did those three knights go?!</i>

15:16.720 --> 15:18.310
<i>Why is no one coming?!</i>

15:18.590 --> 15:21.940
You get to die by one of the
 Sacred Swords you cherish so much.

15:22.240 --> 15:25.820
I would've thought you'd look happier.

15:29.050 --> 15:31.450
I'll be joining you soon enough.

15:32.000 --> 15:34.530
Wait for me in the afterlife.

15:36.900 --> 15:41.000
Then it really was Cardinal Clavwell.

15:41.310 --> 15:43.150
You knew?

15:43.150 --> 15:45.140
I had my suspicions.

15:45.140 --> 15:48.670
He's always had absolute faith in 
the righteousness of the Church.

15:48.970 --> 15:54.430
Asinine. No one who goes around waving the 
flag of justice ever lives up to their own claims.

15:55.100 --> 15:57.640
You're always such a harsh judge.

15:58.070 --> 16:01.160
I do think the Church has 
taken a strange turn.

16:01.160 --> 16:03.900
But, I want to change it, 
even if only a bit at a time.

16:04.540 --> 16:06.610
Which is why I'll be going back.

16:06.970 --> 16:07.940
I see.

16:09.960 --> 16:12.610
By the way, that tea is poisoned.

16:14.770 --> 16:16.010
I was joking.

16:16.010 --> 16:19.500
But you need to learn to be more suspicious 
or it's likely to happen again.

16:20.910 --> 16:23.750
I get your point, but wasn't 
that in poor taste?!

16:23.750 --> 16:27.480
I almost spilled the tea that Nephy prepared!

16:27.480 --> 16:30.720
Nephy wasn't the one who made it.

16:39.280 --> 16:43.740
We never did get to have a 
proper conversation, did we?

16:48.320 --> 16:51.740
Well, I don't expect us to 
necessarily get along, considering...

16:52.640 --> 16:53.580
I should go.

16:55.370 --> 16:57.280
Come visit again, Chastille.

17:01.410 --> 17:05.500
Oh, good! You finally used my real name!

17:01.410 --> 17:07.420
<b>Wahhhh</b>

17:05.500 --> 17:07.420
And you cried anyway?

17:07.790 --> 17:10.430
It wasn't for long, 
but I appreciate you letting me stay.

17:10.430 --> 17:13.630
I'm not sure I can head up something 
like a reconciliation faction,

17:13.630 --> 17:18.310
but I'll do whatever I can to make the 
world a better place for all of you!

17:18.310 --> 17:21.780
Indeed! I'm pleased to see
 you've finally found your resolve.

17:22.830 --> 17:25.400
Should you need help, simply ask.

17:25.400 --> 17:28.060
Of course. I appreciate it, Sir Raphael.

17:31.680 --> 17:34.240
Should you be up already, Raphael?

17:34.240 --> 17:37.700
Quite. Considering the blessing 
I received from Orobas,

17:38.000 --> 17:42.830
the addition of elvish healing made 
my wounds barely an inconvenience.

17:42.830 --> 17:47.080
How are you two chatting so casually?!

17:47.480 --> 17:49.010
Is there some problem?

17:49.010 --> 17:52.590
I mean, I thought he was dead!

17:52.590 --> 17:56.380
Who do you think told me
 about what happened to Clavwell?

17:52.590 --> 17:57.090
<b>I **lled him.</b>

17:57.090 --> 18:00.680
<b>It wasn't For</b>

17:57.380 --> 17:59.620
I also prepared the tea.

18:02.420 --> 18:05.850
Still, I'm glad to see you're alive!

18:05.850 --> 18:11.560
<b>Menace...</b>

18:06.160 --> 18:07.920
So naïve.

18:07.920 --> 18:11.560
If you keep this up, you're likely to 
be struck down when you least expect it.

18:11.560 --> 18:15.030
Well, considering you could be betrayed 
at any moment by just about anyone,

18:15.030 --> 18:17.180
you can't go around so obliviously.

18:17.180 --> 18:18.650
That's his point.

18:18.650 --> 18:20.340
Well said, my lord.

18:21.090 --> 18:23.280
Even I understood that time.

18:23.870 --> 18:25.540
Wait, "my lord"?

18:25.890 --> 18:29.070
I have been hired to serve 
as Lord Zagan's butler.

18:29.070 --> 18:31.840
As of today, I am no longer 
commander of the Angelic Knights.

18:34.450 --> 18:39.260
<i>The barrier detected him when Raphael 
collapsed on the outside of the castle.</i>

18:39.260 --> 18:43.260
I've come to offer my head, as promised.

18:43.740 --> 18:45.000
What do you think, For?

18:45.680 --> 18:46.880
It's your decision.

18:52.240 --> 18:55.810
In that case, you should 
serve Zagan and Nephy.

18:55.810 --> 18:57.610
That will help me, too.

19:00.270 --> 19:02.700
<i>Having a Sacred Sword and its wielder nearby</i>

19:02.700 --> 19:06.480
<i>will make a huge difference in my 
studies on the Archdemon brand.</i>

19:06.480 --> 19:09.860
Mr. Raphael's quite a cook, as well!

19:09.860 --> 19:11.830
I'm thinking about having him teach me.

19:12.070 --> 19:15.810
<i>Plus, he's weirdly easy to relate to.</i>

19:20.800 --> 19:22.920
Do you miss your arm?

19:22.920 --> 19:25.490
It's nothing for you to 
concern yourself with.

19:25.490 --> 19:26.750
Wait a minute.

19:36.800 --> 19:38.940
It should move, too.

19:39.390 --> 19:41.800
That's the armor I used as Valefor.

19:43.530 --> 19:48.240
To think I would owe so much to not 
just Orobas, but his daughter also...

19:48.630 --> 19:50.790
I shall dedicate my life to serving you.

19:51.000 --> 19:51.750
Hmph

19:51.520 --> 19:52.670
Overreacting...

19:52.970 --> 19:56.840
Wait, so I'm the only one who's moving out?

19:57.080 --> 19:58.210
Looks like it.

20:00.030 --> 20:02.420
You can drop by any time you want.

20:02.420 --> 20:04.050
I'm sure Nephy and For 
would be glad to see you.

20:04.480 --> 20:05.840
I would?

20:05.840 --> 20:06.930
Sure you would.

20:07.430 --> 20:08.430
What about you, Zagan?

20:10.000 --> 20:13.770
Well, you make decent enough 
company to share a drink with.

20:17.410 --> 20:18.940
See you later!

20:19.250 --> 20:22.280
Honestly, she makes such a fuss.

20:22.670 --> 20:25.360
Aren't you guys forgetting somebody?

20:27.230 --> 20:30.830
Not that I care. 
That was a nice nap, but I'm starving!

20:31.290 --> 20:33.480
How about some breakfast?

20:33.480 --> 20:35.610
Actually, I need you to go, too.

20:36.260 --> 20:39.050
Chastille could use protecting 
for the time being.

20:39.050 --> 20:40.840
I mean, did you see how she acted?

20:41.450 --> 20:43.810
What am I, a babysitter?

20:43.810 --> 20:46.720
Stop whining. You'll be paid.

20:46.720 --> 20:49.980
Besides, you left the tab to me last time.

20:49.980 --> 20:54.730
Y'know, buddy, you really oughta take 
better care of your talented friends!

21:06.800 --> 21:07.570
Nephy?

21:07.920 --> 21:09.990
Wh-What are you upset about?

21:09.990 --> 21:12.080
Is that how I seem?

21:12.490 --> 21:14.830
That's why I was asking, yes.

21:19.410 --> 21:22.920
In that case... try and understand.

21:23.310 --> 21:27.800
<i>This... She's upset, but 
also expecting something?</i>

21:28.310 --> 21:31.060
<i>This is a tricky one! But...</i>

21:33.330 --> 21:34.390
Uh, well...

21:37.280 --> 21:40.480
I'm sorry I left you behind last night.

21:41.470 --> 21:45.190
Lord Zagan... that's not playing fair.

21:49.510 --> 21:51.960
I can't see, Raphael.

21:51.960 --> 21:55.080
For, my dear, you're still too 
young for this kind of thing.

23:30.010 --> 23:35.010
<b>Next Time: 
Music At Night Is Lovely, But May Be 
Too Much When You're Socially Awkward</b>
